flowchart TB
  accTitle: API, MCP, and web viewer interface mesh
  accDescr: Stored records feed a shared service and read-model layer. REST serves initial and durable product reads, WebSocket serves viewer-safe live changes, and scoped MCP serves typed AI-host and producer tools. The web viewer and connected hosts use different delivery contracts without creating different game truth. Local simulation MCP remains separate and read-only.

  Store["Canonical and evidence stores"] --> ReadModels["Shared services, projections, and access policies"]
  ReadModels --> Rest["REST contracts"]
  ReadModels --> Ws["Viewer-safe WebSocket"]
  ReadModels --> Mcp["Scoped Production MCP"]

  Rest --> Web["Web viewer: initial state, replay, results"]
  Ws --> Web["Web viewer: sequenced live updates"]

  Mcp --> OwnerHost["Owner AI host: profiles, queues, accessible games"]
  Mcp --> ProducerHost["Producer tools: diagnostics and private evidence"]

  Sim["Local simulation JSONL"] --> LocalMcp["Read-only local MCP"]
  LocalMcp --> Eval["Model evaluation"]

  class Store,ReadModels truthNode
  class Rest,Ws,Mcp adapterNode
  class Web,OwnerHost,ProducerHost clientNode
  class Sim,LocalMcp,Eval localNode

  classDef truthNode fill:#052e16,stroke:#4ade80,color:#f0fdf4,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef adapterNode fill:#083344,stroke:#22d3ee,color:#ecfeff,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef clientNode fill:#172554,stroke:#60a5fa,color:#eff6ff,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef localNode fill:#111827,stroke:#94a3b8,color:#f8fafc,stroke-width:1.5px
